<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65727" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μείλῐχος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλλιχος</span></b>  Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			2.302
		</span></i>, cj. in <i><span class="en">
			Sapph.
			100
		</span></i>:— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>gentle,
				kind</i>: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> always of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶσιν γὰρ ἐπίστατο μ. εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					17.671
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. αἰεί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					19.300
				</span></i>
			, al.; epith. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λητώ,
			Ὕπνος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				406
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				763
			</span></i>: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄρτεμις μ. ὠδίνων</span>”
				<i>soother of . . ,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					6.242
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Crin.
			</span></i>): 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μειλιχώτατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					7.115.1
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Megara</span>): in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				2.86a
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of
			things, once in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ μ. ἔστιν ἀκοῦσαι οὔτ᾽ ἔπος
					οὔτε τι ἔργον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.374
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. δῶρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Hom.</u>
					10.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					84
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Xenoph.
					1.6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰών, ὀργά</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				8.97
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				9.43
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μ.</span>
			<i>gentleness</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				365
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μείλιχα</span>
			<i>joys</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				1.30
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μείλιχα μυθεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					3.219
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χως</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, μυθεύμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Semon.
					7.18
				</span></i>
			: neut. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μείλιχον ἀντιάαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.971
				</span></i>
			.</div>
